# Slides + Notes Presenter — feature plan

> Feature slug: `presenter`
> Goal: a single-page app that loads any existing HTML catechism deck and lets the presenter see slide notes while presenting. Three viewing modes, read-only notes, sidecar JSON storage.
> Decisions (locked by user 2025-10-05):
> 1. Notes live in `*.notes.json` sidecar files, paired by slide index. No edits to deck HTML.
> 2. Three note UX modes, all shipped: presenter window (second monitor), in-page side panel, toggle overlay (`N`).
> 3. Read-only inside the app. Notes edited in the user's editor of choice.

## Non-goals

- No editing of notes inside the app (read-only per user decision).
- No auth, no upload, no remote hosting.
- No modifications to existing decks.
- No fullscreen presentation quirks like kezels — keep first cut simple.

## Architecture

- `presenter.html` — main shell + popup shell (differentiated by `?popup=1` URL param).
- `presenter.js` — main app logic (deck loader, nav, hotkeys, modes).
- `presenter-shared.js` — pure helpers (slide parsing, scaling math, sidecar parsing, BroadcastChannel protocol). Dual-exported for Node `node --test` and the browser.
- `serve.sh` — launcher using `python3 -m http.server` (browser can't `fetch()` JSON over `file://`).
- `tests/presenter-shared.test.js` — Node `node --test` suite for pure helpers.
- `README.md` — usage, keyboard cheatsheet, sidecar format.

## Deck loading strategy

- `fetch()` the deck HTML as text.
- Parse with `DOMParser`.
- Extract all `<style>` blocks → re-inject as `<style>` elements into a scoped `<div id="deck-styles">` (so multiple decks could be cached without CSS bleed).
- Drop every `<script>` (we own it).
- Extract every `<section class="slide">` from inside the deck's `.stage` → clone into my own `.stage`.
- Add `.is-active` to slide 0.
- Scale-to-fit the stage at 1920×1080 with the same math the original decks used.

## Sidecar format

```json
{
  "deck": "catechism-deck-dios-padre-creador-3",
  "slides": [
    "Notes for slide 1. Plain text or light markdown.",
    "Notes for slide 2..."
  ]
}
```

- Looked up at `<deck>.notes.json` in the same directory as the HTML.
- If `slides.length < total`, pad with empty strings.
- If file missing, show a copyable empty template and an "Open in editor" hint pointing at the path.

## Notes UX

- **Overlay drawer (default toggle)**: press `N`. Right-side drawer slides in, ~360px wide, slide reflows. Press `N` or click outside to close.
- **In-page side panel**: toggle from menu. Persistent split. Stage left, notes right, with a draggable splitter.
- **Presenter window**: press `W`. Opens `presenter.html?popup=1&deck=...&index=...` in a popup. Popup shows current notes, current slide thumbnail, next slide thumbnail, total time + per-slide time. Sync via `BroadcastChannel('slideschurch')` with messages `{type:'goto', index, notes, slides, deck}`.

## Hotkeys

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `→` `Space` `PageDown` | Next slide |
| `←` `PageUp` | Previous slide |
| `Home` | First slide |
| `End` | Last slide |
| `N` | Toggle notes drawer |
| `W` | Open presenter window |
| `F` | Toggle browser fullscreen |
| `?` | Toggle help overlay |
| `Esc` | Close drawer / help / exit fullscreen |

